  "vertical_metrics": {
    "date": "2026-09-11",
    "cause": "a synthesized weight (the theme font ships one file; `h1` is 600) was a derived face without the primary's bytes, so face_metrics took FreeType's pixel-sized path -- ceil(ascent) + ceil(descent) -- while the regular face took the design-rounded path Blink uses: for Open Sans SemiBold at 32px that is 35 + 10 = 45 against Blink's 34 + 9 = 43, the two-pixel h1 height finding, and the one-pixel y shifts below it",
    "fix": "GodotFontBackend::variant records the base's bytes for the derived handle, so face_metrics rounds its design extents the same way (godot_font.cpp)",
    "font_check": "fontTools on the harness font: upem 2048, hhea ascent 2189 / descent -600 / lineGap 0, USE_TYPO_METRICS set with the same typo values; at 32px design ascent 34.203 and descent 9.375",
